              %strong Abstract.
            %p
              For
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
              %a{:href => "higher+gauge+field#HigherGaugeTheoryOfMaxwellType"} of Maxwell type
              — e.g. the common
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
              (the “A-field”) but also the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} C-fields
              considered in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              —
              = succeed "&" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+quantization"} -quantization
              laws specify
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative completions
              of these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
              by encoding their
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} solitonic
              behaviour and hence by specifying the quantized
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charges"} charges
              carried by the individual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
              that source these fluxes (higher-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
              or
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solitons"} solitons
            %p
              This page surveys the general (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"}> rational
              \-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretic
              understanding &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#FSS23"}> FSS23-Char
              \&amp;rbrack; of flux- &amp; charge-quantization via the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Dold+character+map"} Chern-Dold character map
              generalized to the
              %em non-linear
              (self-sourcing)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
              that appear in higher-dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              theories, notably for
              = succeed "&" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-
