            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/GeomPhys-HigherGaugeFieldAsHomotopy.jpg", :width => "350px"}/
          %p
            More in detail, a
            %em flux-quantized higher gauge field
            is (i) a flux density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec B
            being a cocycle in
            = succeed "-de" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} rchi
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rchi
            being a cocycle in
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potential"} gauge potential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat A
            being a coboundary between their joint images (thus exhibiting the above identification of their cohomology classes).
          %p
            This makes the flux-quantized higher gauge fields be cocycles in
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+nonabelian+cohomology"} differential
            = succeed "-cohomology." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
          %p
