          %p
          #RoleOfLInfinityAlgebras.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (the role of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                    \-algebras
              %br/
              In comparison to more traditional discussions, beware that the (possibly non-abelian)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              here controls the (possibly non-linear)
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gauss+law"} Gauss law
              satisfied by the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature+forms"} curvature forms
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+densities"} flux densities
              — and thus is
              %em not
              the (higher) Lie algebra in which the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+potentials"} gauge potentials
              take values, if any. (Even in the abelian case, where both types of coefficient
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %p
              This is an underappreciated use of
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "L-infinity-algebra#ReferencesInPhysics"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  \-algebras in physics
              %a{:href => "D'Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} “FDA”-method in supergravity
              and is tacitly familiar in traditional discussion of RR-flux/D-brane charge:
            %p
              Here the characteristic
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [b_2, \, v_{2\bullet-1}] = v_{2\bullet + 1}
              bears no resemblance to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+unitary+Lie+algebra"}
