              %a{:href => "higher+gauge+field#OfChernSimonsType"} higher Chern-Simons type theories
              are different.
          %p
          #MotionOfElectromagneticField.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (Motion of the ordinary electromagnetic fluxes)
            %p
              The classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxwell+equations"} Maxwell equations
              expressed in terms of differential forms (see basic references
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Maxwell's+equations#ReferencesForMaxwellEquationsViaDifferentialForms"} here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/premetric+electromagnetism"} premetric
              form shown on the right (see the references
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "pre-metric+electromagnetism#ReferencesPremetricElectromagnetism"} there
            %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 0px"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/GeomPhys-MotionOfElectromagnetism.jpg", :width => "430px"}/
            %p
              Here the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+3-form"} differential 3-form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
