                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CE}(\mathfrak{g})
            whose cochain cohomology computes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            (with trivial coefficients) — but the key point at the moment is that its construction is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} embedding
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite
            of that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
